WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.335 --> 00:00:04.295
One small step for man, 

00:00:04.295 --> 00:00:07.507
one giant leap for Finch Weinberg.

00:00:10.468 --> 00:00:14.556
Hello. We have Caleb Landry Jones as Jeff.

00:00:14.806 --> 00:00:19.811
He had to wear these huge stilts,
 all this other CGI friendly stuff.

00:00:20.186 --> 00:00:23.815
We used Mo-Cap, a Moven suit, which is
 a suit that records all of your movements.

00:00:24.816 --> 00:00:27.819
There's a hand-off
 between the Legacy puppeteers

00:00:27.819 --> 00:00:30.780
who are starting the evolution
 of the artificial intelligence,

00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:35.577
and then visual effects takes over
 by having a bunch of animators

00:00:35.577 --> 00:00:40.040
and Caleb as an actor
 evolving the artificial intelligence.

00:00:40.415 --> 00:00:44.919
So, Legacy, they've built a robot that's
 the most complex robot they've ever built.

00:00:45.128 --> 00:00:48.715
There is enormous amount of parts
 that were created for these puppets.

00:00:49.382 --> 00:00:52.052
Jeff was really very different
 from other robots that we've done

00:00:52.052 --> 00:00:55.055
in the past with let's bring him
 and ground him in the real world.

00:00:55.513 --> 00:00:58.892
So his head is the top
 of a welding gas tank.

00:00:58.892 --> 00:01:01.061
A lot of his body parts, it's all chipped.

00:01:01.186 --> 00:01:02.771
There's a lot of different textures. 

00:01:02.771 --> 00:01:06.649
It was very important that we actually
 had a physical robot on set.

00:01:08.401 --> 00:01:12.655
Once Jeff becomes a fully formed
 robot, Caleb then takes over.

00:01:13.865 --> 00:01:17.494
It was good to make sure
 that before you had Jeff become a fully CG

00:01:17.494 --> 00:01:21.039
character, that you introduce
 a character to the audience

00:01:21.039 --> 00:01:24.209
that is grounded in reality
 and in the real world.

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:30.048
When I saw it recently,
 I didn't remember Caleb in costume.

00:01:30.256 --> 00:01:33.218
I was just seeing Jeff as Jeff,
 a testament, I think, to

00:01:33.510 --> 00:01:36.346
how fluid Caleb was inside all of that.

00:01:38.306 --> 00:01:41.059
You can't really get the nuances
 of what happens on set,

00:01:41.059 --> 00:01:44.145
if it was just a CG thing
 that worked perfectly every single time.

00:01:47.607 --> 00:01:51.236
There's this amazing creature
 that's not part of our normal life,

00:01:51.236 --> 00:01:54.948
but that's just kind of this horror to tell a very, very human story.

